[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126217,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hidradenoma papilliferum is a benign tumour associated with anogenital mammary-like glands, characterized by branching and interconnecting epithelial and stromal elements, microscopically resembling mammary intraductal papilloma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126218,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8405/0 Hidradenoma papilliferum</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126219,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F22 &amp; XH4DX4 Benign neoplasms of epidermal appendages &amp; Papillary hidradenoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126220,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> papillary hidradenoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126221,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126222,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases affect the vulva; less frequently, the perianal and perineal skin is involved.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126223,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesion occurs as a solitary asymptomatic nodule or cyst-like lesion measuring 2&ndash;20&nbsp;mm {26863059}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126224,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hidradenoma papilliferum is the most common benign glandular neoplasm of the vulva. It almost exclusively affects White women aged 20&ndash;89&nbsp;years; it occurs rarely in children and in Black populations {10411423; 10986678}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126225,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hidradenoma papilliferum is thought to arise from anogenital mammary-like glands {8005737}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126226,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumorigenic alterations in the PI3K/AKT and MAPK pathway have been identified {28291131; 28648934; 27184479; 31010589; 26493284}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126227,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is typically a tan or red nodule with a solid to variably cystic cut surface.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126228,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hidradenoma papilliferum appears as a well-circumscribed intradermal solid-cystic nodule with a complex pattern of branching and anastomosing tubules interconnected in a labyrinthine manner, focally forming papillae. The tubules and papillae consist of a central axis of fibrous tissue lined by a luminal layer of epithelial cells surrounded by a layer of myoepithelial cells. Decapitation secretion is common.</p>\r\n<p>Cystic change, sclerosing adenosis&ndash;like and mammary-type ductal changes, and necrosis have been identified. Oxyphilic metaplasia, especially in areas with solid growth with nuclear polymorphism, may simulate adenocarcinoma. Remnants of anogenital mammary-like gland adjacent to the lesion can be seen {26863059}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126229,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 833,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 776,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126230,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 776,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 836,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 779,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126231,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 779,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a solitary asymptomatic nodule or cyst-like lesion; complex growth of branching and anastomosing epithelial papillae and tubules with a myoepithelial cell layer.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 834,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 777,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126232,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 777,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 835,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 778,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 126233,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 154,
        "headingId": 778,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a benign neoplasm. Cases of carcinoma (including ductal carcinoma in&nbsp;situ) arising in hidradenoma papilliferum have been reported {33908057; 34926767; 1662944; 18580327; 18645314}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-24T18:44:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]